  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nWidespread rain will work into the region overnight and into \nThanksgiving morning. Rain will continue through the day and into \nThursday night. Some wet snow may mix in with the rain Thursday night\ninto Friday morning. Temperatures will generally be just above \nfreezing although a few spots may drop to freezing. Due to the \ntemperatures generally above freezing, expect any accumulations to be\nlight and mainly on grassy surfaces. The best chance for these minor\naccumulations would be across eastern Indiana and into west central \nOhio. Rain will be possible at times on Friday before tapering off in\nthe evening.\n\nBreezy conditions will be present on Thursday through Friday with the\nhighest gusts expected to be around the middle of the day on\nThanksgiving. Wind gusts of 35 to 40 mph will be possible during this\ntime. Continue to mention the potential for gusty winds in the HWO.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nDry conditions are expected on Saturday. Rain chances return Sunday\nmorning and remain across the region until Sunday night. Dry\nconditions return for Monday and into the beginning of next week.",
